# Completion review — add-apinex-zero-price-source

**Status:** Local source implementation, focused tests, OpenSpec validation, and
independent review are complete. Combined TL322/TL324 release and native
free-only live acceptance remain open; this package stays unarchived.

## Cause and source

The configured APInex node already had imported raw model IDs, but the native
pricing namespace and strict-zero snapshot had no APInex source. The existing
exact provider/model guard therefore had no source evidence for APInex IDs.

On 2026-10-29, the official public structured catalog at
[`/api/public/models`](https://apinex.bond/api/public/models) returned 44 model
rows with raw `id`, numeric `dollarsPer1M` input price, and numeric
`outputDollarsPer1M` output price. The official [catalog page](https://apinex.bond/models?provider=Free)
showed 21 zero-price rows. The adapter uses only structured numeric price and
raw identity fields; `provider`, `name`, `allowFree`, health, and `free/` prefix
do not create price evidence.

## Change

- Fetch APInex only when an exact configured OpenAI-compatible chat node uses
  `https://api.apinex.bond/v1`.
- Require a complete nonempty catalog, unique raw IDs, and finite non-negative
  numeric price fields. Only records with numeric zero for input, output, and
  every additional published per-token price field qualify.
- Intersect exact catalog IDs with IDs already present under that node's
  `syncedAvailableModels` connections. Do not write availability, visibility,
  exclusion, connection, capability, fitness, or candidate data.
- Persist only current APInex provenance in a separate snapshot. Preserve it
  across models.dev saves without changing its timestamp; independently omit
  stale, future, or invalid sources at the existing evidence read and compose
  with the oldest included source timestamp.
- Leave `strictZeroCostFilter.ts` and strict policy unchanged. A malformed or
  failed APInex fetch does not fail a successful models.dev pricing or
  capability sync.

## Verification

- RED was observed before the APInex adapter existed: the focused test failed
  with `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND` for `src/lib/modelsDevSync/apinex.ts`.
- Focused models.dev and APInex tests pass **33/33**, including current-source
  parsing, exact identity binding, unavailable/paid/mixed IDs, stale/future and
  exact 36-hour boundaries, APInex-only read, source failure/empty response,
  next models.dev save, and clear behavior.
- `npx --yes @fission-ai/openspec@latest validate add-apinex-zero-price-source --strict`
  passes.
- Prettier and `git diff --check` pass for changed files.
- `npm run typecheck:core` exits 2 with 720 project diagnostics outside changed
  files; it reports no diagnostics for `src/lib/modelsDevSync.ts`,
  `src/lib/modelsDevSync/apinex.ts`, or the changed test.
- Code Simplifier review applied to the implementation and test diff.
- Fresh independent Luna-high review found no concrete code or policy findings.

## Remaining acceptance

The source package is local-only. TL322 canonical identity work and TL324
pricing work must be coordinated together for release. No GitHub push, build,
deployment, provider probe, or model completion was performed here. The
original native free-only acceptance remains pending: one successful controlled
call must prove model, connection, route, usage, and zero cost with no paid or
out-of-band fallback. Track this gate in `openspec/TODO.md`.
